  "details": "Add the ability for avatar/world creators and shader developers to respond to selected client preferences.\n\n(Similar to how websites are able to tell if you're using high contrast or reduced motion)\n\nAs a result, avatar/world creators could show a less detailed mesh, according to a client's performance preferences and even disable features (like realtime lights) entirely.\n\nAdditionally, shader developers could use this metric to replace complex effect with simplified versions, optimized for lower end hardware.\n\nThis would reduce the need to block shaders or animations in order to maintain a playable framerate on lower-end systems.\n\nThese performance preferences would also be used to reduce the detail of far away avatars or even respond to the amount of players in the current world. (Thus improving performance during large events)",
